35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"It turns out we're losing nearly an hour a day to copying records, and there are several misrouted deliveries because different units have different addresses for the same firms.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"That's a lot of wasted time, but my findings are worrying. Our in-house developers are tied up until Q3, and the coordination group is severely understaffed.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"To add to that, network coverage at customer plants is unreliable, with some losing signal for whole afternoons, and vendor pricing for licenses scales up per person, which could get expensive.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital budget is frozen, though we have some room in the software allowance. Also, vendor queries are being handled inefficiently, with the same certificates requested multiple times.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found out that tools requiring daily entry from everyone were dropped in the last three rollouts, and most cross-unit standardization efforts ended without an owner. Only the tool room walkthroughs are still used!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if the developers are busy and the coordination group is understaffed, we should be very careful about any proposal that requires a lot of internal setup or manual maintenance.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. We can't afford a project that adds more burden to the few people we have left, or one that relies on developers who aren't available.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, given the frozen capital budget and the per-head license costs I found, we should probably avoid any proposal that requires a large upfront investment or a scaling subscription model.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. We should prioritize solutions that fit within the recurring software allowance and avoid those that would trigger a capital expenditure request we cannot fulfill.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, your point about the daily losses is key, but we must remember that tools requiring everyone's daily input usually fail here. We need something that solves those problems without becoming another abandoned project.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I see your point, @Kenji. We need a solution that addresses the copying and delivery errors but doesn't rely on a high-maintenance daily routine that people will just stop doing.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"And we must avoid anything that requires our in-house developers immediately. If a proposal needs a custom build right now, it's a non-starter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, we should also be wary of any proposal that assumes seamless connectivity at customer sites, given the signal gaps I discovered. That could be a fatal flaw for certain types of apps.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"That is a critical observation, @Shunichi. Any proposal relying on real-time cloud synchronization at customer plants would be fundamentally flawed and likely to fail in practice.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm starting to think we need a project that is narrow in scope and has a clear owner, since the broad standardization efforts usually just vanish into thin air.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree with @Kenji. A focused tool that solves a specific, tangible problem—like the record copying or the address errors—seems much safer than a massive overhaul.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,I agree. Let's look for something that doesn't require a huge team to maintain or a massive amount of developer time to launch.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll be looking for a proposal that avoids the per-head license trap and doesn't assume our technicians have a perfect signal in the field. That should narrow it down.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I will be looking for a proposal that fits within the software allowance and avoids capital expenditure, while addressing the inefficiencies in how we handle vendor and supplier data.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'll be looking for something that doesn't require everyone to use it every single day, or it'll just end up like the last three failures!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
