60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Looking at the candidates, the Supplier Data Hub seems to address the misrouted deliveries and the redundant vendor queries Ryuji mentioned, without requiring daily input from everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"The Supplier Data Hub sounds promising, but I'm worried about the developer availability. If it requires a custom build, we're stuck until Q3. Does it look like a vendor product or an in-house build?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The Field Service App is out because of the network gaps I found. The Supplier Data Hub is better, provided it doesn't use those per-head licenses that scale with every department.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The Supplier Data Hub aligns with the software allowance and solves the vendor query issue. It is a central repository, which suggests a more manageable cost structure than a per-head license.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"The Supplier Data Hub is a narrow tool for a specific problem, which fits the pattern of what actually survives here, unlike the Workflow Assistant which sounds like it requires daily entry from everyone.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the Supplier Data Hub is a central repository for records, which might be easier to implement than a full app, and it directly fixes the address errors I found.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"I'm still concerned about the coordination group, but a central hub for supplier records seems less demanding than a full-scale app or a training studio. It feels like the most sustainable option.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the Supplier Data Hub is a consolidated catalog, it likely avoids the connectivity issues of the Field Service App and the high maintenance of the Workflow Assistant. It seems the most rational choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. It addresses the inefficiencies in vendor data handling and fits our financial constraints, making it the most logical and prudent selection among the candidates.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm on board! It's a specific fix for a real problem, and it doesn't sound like it'll be abandoned like those broad standardization projects. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with everyone. It solves the daily losses I found without being too ambitious. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,It seems to be the only one that won't break our staff or our budget. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It is the only proposal that survives the constraints we've identified. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It is the most reasonable choice given the budget and the operational inefficiencies. I vote for the Supplier Data Hub.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
